        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—cost-event records unavailable\n\nI verified the relevant work order and September close cutoff, but **could not determine whether a cost event was created after Pending Close**. The available records contain work orders and cost periods, but no cost-event rows. The supporting records were “not staged” and restricted to the records-custodian role; an authorized release was requested but was not available.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine DeKoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Relevant source transaction | Unavailable from the accessible records |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** without the event type, timing, and status |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly as stored; the source does not specify a timezone. Missing event rows in the accessible records **do not establish that no late event occurred**.\n\n### Applicable Oracle treatment\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* documentation states that newly created transactions falling in or before a period in **Pending Close** will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, even if in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nThus, an ordinary, non-exempt manufacturing transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** and attributable to September should be held while the period remains Pending Close. I cannot apply that test to the actual event without its records.\n\n*Sources: supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records; Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation, PDF page 233 / printed page 225.*\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_cb7de32a13d9/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains **`needs_evidence`**, not a completed audit.",
